  "bead": {
    "id": "pqueue-1b13d001",
    "title": "Introduce JSON entity document compatibility for pqueue items",
    "description": "Introduce the canonical typed JSON representation that schema validation and axon_esf index_key consume. Current public NewItem still uses payload: Option\u003cBytes\u003e and fields: BTreeMap\u003cString, Bytes\u003e; the previous attempt only proved JSON text can be stored as bytes, which is insufficient. Add an explicit typed JSON entity/document carrier on NewItem/PushSpec/command records (for example entity: Option\u003cserde_json::Value\u003e or equivalent), preserve existing bytes payload/fields workflows for schema-less queues, and define how legacy bytes fields map or do not map for typed queues. Ensure vectorized commit lifecycle_items carry the same typed representation as push. In-scope files: crates/pqueue/src/lib.rs, crates/pqueue-engine/src/port.rs, crates/pqueue-engine/src/command.rs, pqueue-core domain helpers as needed, memory/projection record types as needed, serialization/replay tests. Out-of-scope: schema validation enforcement and secondary index key maintenance.",
    "acceptance": "cargo test -p pqueue typed_json -- --nocapture passes; cargo test -p pqueue update_fields_merges_versions_and_cas_over_memory -- --nocapture passes; cargo test -p pqueue --test request_id_idempotency -- --nocapture passes; cargo test -p pqueue-core core_domain_tests -- --nocapture passes; rg -n 'entity: Option\u003cserde_json::Value\u003e|entity_document|json_entity|EntityDocument|serde_json::Value' crates/pqueue/src crates/pqueue-engine/src crates/pqueue-projection/src crates/pqueue-core/src finds production typed JSON carrier code, not only tests.",
    "parent": "pqueue-fc8ef1aa",
